A pipe input's cover art survives a pause.

The cover that arrives through the metadata pipe is kept in a temporary
file the queue item's artwork_url points at, and the file was removed
whenever the metadata pipe stopped being watched. That happens on every
pause, because a pause stops the input and sets it up again. From then on
the artwork API answered 404 for the item, the speakers were sent nothing,
and the next PICT only comes with the next track. The file now lives
until the next picture replaces it or the input module deinitialises.

